JIT: Compare the initialized CRC accumulator for empty code entries.

A failed decode can produce a zero-length entry. ValidateCode initializes
its accumulator to zero but only writes TMP1 for nonempty code. Comparing
TMP1 unconditionally repeatedly invalidates the empty entry. Compare the
actual accumulator, preserving all nonempty behavior. Bump the disk-cache
version so previously generated validation code is discarded.

Regression: tests/x64-fidelity/memtest.c with FEX_SMCCHECKS=full and
FEX_DISKCACHE=0. Before: hangs at access.noaccess.execute, even with 0025.
After: 51 pass / 0 fail with Wine's mapped-execute correction; 50/0 with
the earlier 50-check test. Normal mode has the same result. FH6 still
exits during startup under full validation; this is not a game fix.

diff --git a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/DiskCache.h b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/DiskCache.h
index ab0264d..0b43365 100644
--- a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/DiskCache.h
+++ b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/DiskCache.h
@@ -249,7 +249,7 @@ namespace DiskCache {
   // The current version of the diskcache.
   // This must be changed any time codegen changes occur!
   // Be aware of the impact of changing this frequently!
-  static constexpr uint16_t FormatVersion = 30;
+  static constexpr uint16_t FormatVersion = 31;
 
   static constexpr uint32_t LOOKUP_KEY_MAX_BUCKET_DEPTH = 500;
 
diff --git a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/JIT/BranchOps.cpp b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/JIT/BranchOps.cpp
index c2b1d8e..116de5d 100644
--- a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/JIT/BranchOps.cpp
+++ b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/JIT/BranchOps.cpp
@@ -362,7 +362,8 @@ DEF_OP(ValidateCode) {
     WorkingReg = TMP1;
   }
 
-  sub(ARMEmitter::Size::i32Bit, Dst, TMP1, CRC32Reg);
+  // Empty decode entries have a zero CRC; TMP1 is only initialized for nonempty code.
+  sub(ARMEmitter::Size::i32Bit, Dst, WorkingReg, CRC32Reg);
 
   ARMEmitter::ForwardLabel End;
   cbz_OrRestart(ARMEmitter::Size::i32Bit, Dst, &End);
